{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — JUDGE.ME CAROUSEL BROKEN-IMAGE GUARD (2026-09-04) ═══

  THE BUG
  Judge.me's review carousel renders some product thumbnails with NO `src`
  attribute at all (verified live: `img.jdgm-carousel-item__product-image`
  with `getAttribute('src') === null` for "Tommy Hilfiger Black Cap" and
  "Jordan Jumpman White T-shirt"). The element still occupies 290x56, so the
  homepage carousel shows blank slots next to real review text.

  It is NOT a catalog gap — both products have images in Shopify
  (lbass-prod-p012-01.jpg, lbass-prod-p014-01.jpg). Judge.me's own cached
  review data is missing the URL, so the ROOT FIX is a product re-sync inside
  the Judge.me app. This snippet only stops the blank box from being shown
  while that is outstanding.

  WHY JS AND NOT CSS
  A plain `img:not([src])` rule would also hide any thumbnail Judge.me
  lazy-loads a moment later, silently deleting good images. This checks
  `naturalWidth === 0` AFTER load instead, so it only ever hides an image that
  genuinely failed. It hides the <img>, never the review, so the customer's
  words and star rating stay on the page.

  Scoped to `.jdgm-carousel-item__product-image` — it cannot touch store imagery.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* collapse the slot rather than leaving a 290x56 gap */
  img.jdgm-carousel-item__product-image[data-lbass-broken="1"]{display:none!important}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  var SEL = 'img.jdgm-carousel-item__product-image';
  function sweep(){
    var imgs = document.querySelectorAll(SEL), n = 0;
    for (var i = 0; i < imgs.length; i++){
      var im = imgs[i];
      var src = im.getAttribute('src');
      var failed = (!src) || (im.complete && im.naturalWidth === 0);
      if (failed){ im.setAttribute('data-lbass-broken', '1'); n++; }
    }
    return n;
  }
  /* the widget is injected async, so sweep a few times then stop */
  var passes = 0;
  var t = setInterval(function(){
    sweep();
    if (++passes >= 10) clearInterval(t);
  }, 700);
  window.addEventListener('load', sweep);
})();
</script>
